face-video","labs":["Apple"],"signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"official_ai_research_catalogue","ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research","matched_terms":["generative model","generative models","generative","neural"],"concept_ids":[],"work_type":"publication"},"ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},{"id":"apple:kg9dyvksb6rothh3mt5j2kpf","title":"Robust Joint Shape and Pose Optimization for Few-view Object Reconstruction","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/robust-joint-shape","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/robust-joint-shape"],"alternate_titles":["Robust Joint Shape and Pose Optimization for Few-view Object Reconstruction"],"published":"2022-06-05","authors":["Zhenpei Yang","Zhile Ren","Miguel Angel Bautista","Zaiwei Zhang","Qi Shan","Qixing Huang"],"abstract":"Reconstructing an accurate 3D object model from a few image observations remains a challenging problem in computer vision. State-of-the-art approaches typically assume accurate camera poses as input, which could be difficult to obtain in realistic settings. In this paper, we present FvOR, a learning-based object reconstruction method that predicts accurate 3D models given a few images with noisy input poses. The core of our approach is a fast and...","companies":["Apple"],"matched_orgs":["Apple"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["official_publication_page"],"source":"official_publication_page","work_type":"publication","doi":"","openalex_id":"","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":52,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Apple"],"concepts":[],"official_report":true,"quality_signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},"evidence":[{"source":"official_publication_page","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/robust-joint-shape","labs":["Apple"],"signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"official_ai_research_catalogue","ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research","matched_terms":["computer vision"],"concept_ids":[],"work_type":"publication"},"ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},{"id":"apple:j7kg0891d8v2uoi131jvvyyx","title":"Efficient Multi-view Stereo via Attention-Driven 2D Convolutions","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/multi-view-stereo","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/multi-view-stereo"],"alternate_titles":["Efficient Multi-view Stereo via Attention-Driven 2D Convolutions"],"published":"2022-06-05","authors":["Zhenpei Yang","Zhile Ren","Qi Shan","Qixing Huang"],"abstract":"Deep learning has made significant impacts on multi-view stereo systems. State-of-the-art approaches typically involve building a cost volume, followed by multiple 3D convolution operations to recover the input image's pixel-wise depth. While such end-to-end learning of plane-sweeping stereo advances public benchmarks' accuracy, they are typically very slow to compute. We present MVS2D, a highly efficient multi-view stereo algorithm that...","companies":["Apple"],"matched_orgs":["Apple"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["official_publication_page"],"source":"official_publication_page","work_type":"publication","doi":"","openalex_id":"","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":52,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Apple"],"concepts":[],"official_report":true,"quality_signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},"evidence":[{"source":"official_publication_page","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/multi-view-stereo","labs":["Apple"],"signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"official_ai_research_catalogue","ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research","matched_terms":["deep learning"],"concept_ids":[],"work_type":"publication"},"ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},{"id":"apple:ks9dt90k0lpgx8tmzagby363","title":"Forward Compatible Training for Large-Scale Embedding Retrieval Systems","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/forward-compatible-training","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/forward-compatible-training"],"alternate_titles":["Forward Compatible Training for Large-Scale Embedding Retrieval Systems"],"published":"2022-06-01","authors":["Vivek Ramanujan","Pavan Kumar Anasosalu Vasu","Ali Farhadi","Oncel Tuzel","Hadi Pouransari"],"abstract":"In visual retrieval systems, updating the embedding model requires recomputing features for every piece of data. This expensive process is referred to as backfilling. Recently, the idea of backward compatible training (BCT) was proposed. To avoid the cost of backfilling, BCT modifies training of the new model to make its representations compatible with those of the old model. However, BCT can significantly hinder the performance of the new model....","companies":["Apple"],"matched_orgs":["Apple"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["official_publication_page"],"source":"official_publication_page","work_type":"publication","doi":"","openalex_id":"","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":52,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Apple"],"concepts":[],"official_report":true,"quality_signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},"evidence":